 within the Vojvodina region. Nestled in the city of Novi Sad, it has become a beacon of knowledge and cultural exchange in Southern Europe, contributing significantly to the academic landscape of the continent. The university's inception coincided with the broader socio-political changes in Yugoslavia, marking a transition towards a more modern educational framework in the region. Notable figures such as the first rector, professor Đorđe Djurković, played essential roles in shaping the institution's mission to promote higher education and research across various disciplines.

